== 1. DETAIL SIGSEGV isolated (probe, world 2 unless stated; exit codes per rank)
torch 2.10.0+cpu Linux  ddp    DETAIL  [-11, -11]  faulthandler: torch/nn/parallel/distributed.py:1265 _ddp_init_helper <- :877 __init__
torch 2.10.0+cpu Linux  ddp    OFF     [0, 0]      gloo_num_threads 2, backend ProcessGroupGloo
torch 2.6.0+cpu  Linux  ddp    DETAIL  [0, 0]      gloo_num_threads 0 (rank 0) / 65609 (rank 1), backend _ProcessGroupWrapper
torch 2.6.0+cpu  Linux  ddp    INFO    [0, 0]      gloo_num_threads 2, backend ProcessGroupGloo
torch 2.6.0+cpu  Linux  ddp    OFF     [0, 0]      gloo_num_threads 2, backend ProcessGroupGloo
torch 2.12.1+cpu Win    gloo   OFF/INFO/DETAIL  [0, 0] each
torch 2.12.1+cpu Win    ddp    OFF/INFO [0, 0]; DETAIL [3221225477, 3221225477] (0xC0000005) at distributed.py:1421 _ddp_init_helper
torch 2.12.1+cpu Win    runner OFF/INFO [0, 0]; DETAIL [3221225477, 3221225477], same frame: the crash is inside DDP(...), before the runner exists
torch 2.12.1+cpu Win    ddp    DETAIL  gloo backend class before DDP: _ProcessGroupWrapper (OFF: ProcessGroupGloo)

Cause (torch source, raw.githubusercontent.com/pytorch/pytorch/<tag>/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/logger.cpp):
Logger::set_env_variables, called from set_construction_data_and_log in DDP's constructor, does
  auto gloo_pg = static_cast<c10d::ProcessGroupGloo*>(reducer_->process_group_->getBackend(BackendType::GLOO).get());
  auto n_threads = gloo_pg->getNumThreads();          // ProcessGroupGloo.hpp: return options_->threads;
identical in v2.6.0 (lines 106-110), v2.10.0 (103-107) and main (103-107) as fetched 2026-11-16.
Under TORCH_DISTRIBUTED_DEBUG=DETAIL the GLOO backend is a _ProcessGroupWrapper, so the cast is undefined
behaviour: on 2.6.0 it reads garbage (0 / 65609 instead of 2) and survives; on 2.10.0 (Linux) and 2.12.1
(Windows) it segfaults. Verdict: upstream torch bug, latent in the CI pin 2.6.0. No Hexa code is involved
(the minimal DDP case has none). Versions 2.7-2.9 not measured.

